From 66710fb97914caeb50f815f0c75845cd55e83fff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 17:26:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ui: kill teal-slab-behind-yellow-text, theme network map,
 parity audit fixes

- THE reported "yellow text highlighted in teal": stock form_style.css
  .FormTable td span{background-color:#475a5f;color:#FFCC00} puts a teal slab
  behind every value span in every settings table - slab removed, yellow kept
- teal sweep: entry fields section 4 missed (input_macaddr_table, devicepin,
  textarea_ssh_table, IPaddr, top-input, query_list, input_option_left,
  optgroup), dropdown list bodies, the .apply_gen strip behind Apply buttons,
  teal panels (MainContent/content_bg/list_table/popup_bg/eula/qrcode/...),
  in-page tab strips, plus dark-on-dark contrast fixes (drword/diagnose)
- network map themed: NM_table canvas, bgcolor=444f53 tiles, statusTitle
  gradient header, statusbody/cards/client icons/inputs/buttons/tbg tables,
  map node icons recolored crimson via filter; theme link baked into all 16
  device-map/*.asp iframe pages (they load framed-in-framed, so the TopBanner
  bake never reached them - this is why the map looked completely stock)
- parity audit (113 TopBanner pages, stock-vs-reaper visible-element probe
  via headless dump-dom): zero interactive elements hidden by theme/shell on
  all 90 mock-renderable pages; 23 fully data-gated pages listed for
  on-router validation

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
